/Users/tiger/.codex/skills/domainry-builder-v1/assets/DEVELOPMENT_TODO.template.md:256:- [ ] Acceptance scenarios use `harness.session_for_case(case)`, `ScenarioGraph`, and `ReasonOracle`: Runtime `GET /identity/principal-context` supplies every canonical selector, fresh per-scenario identities/records isolate setup, a positive case names and observes its target with required non-empty facts, a negative case reaches its intended stable status/error/concealment and proves unchanged state, and `setup_failed`/`blocked_dependency` cannot be recorded as a downstream product pass or failure
/Users/tiger/.codex/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:137:- **Handler positive coverage is symmetric and DIRECT**: every Handler Action also needs a positive scenario whose `actions` list references it directly with an allowed role (`ledger.action_positive_scenario_missing`). Coverage through a Workflow branch that invokes the Handler does not count — a scheduler-driven or approval-driven Handler still needs one direct positive probe (e.g. the operator role invoking it with an explicit payload).
/Users/tiger/.codex/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:145:Their nested shapes are closed too. `expected_records[]` accepts only `object_key`, `record_key`, `field_key`, `state`, `count`, and `values`; it has no `scope`. `expected_reports[]` accepts only `report_key`, `expected_run`, `expected_export`, `filters`, and array-valued `metrics` (use `[]`, not `{}`, when no metric is asserted). Assertions accept only their published typed assertion fields.
/Users/tiger/.codex/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:157:A positive scenario's referenced seed records must already satisfy every source-owned Handler precondition needed for the expected success path. Every positive or denied role used by executable acceptance must have a project-declared `demo_users[]` identity. Bind a specific identity through `actor`; when an automatic standard case only has a role, that role must have exactly one demo user or exactly one user marked `acceptance_default:true`. The default applies across both `role_key` and `role_keys`; alphabetical order is never identity resolution. A role label alone is not a login. Keep separate negative business-precondition scenarios when that rejection matters. Denied authorization scenarios remain distinct and must fail at the Runtime authorization boundary.
/Users/tiger/.codex/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:159:When a positive Action needs a value the standard runner cannot derive, declare the runner-owned fixture in that scenario's open `config` map: `"action_payloads":[{"action_key":"<declared scenario action>","fields":{"<payload key>":{"value":<typed scalar>}}}]`. An omitted `encoding` requires a literal conforming exactly to the declared scalar payload type; relation/reference literals accept only `$record:<seed-key>` of the declared target, and user literals accept only `$actor`. The existing `{"encoding":"json","value":<array or object>}` form remains available only for `text`/`long_text`, resolving nested `$record:<seed-key>` values before canonical JSON encoding. The Action must belong to that positive scenario, actor plus Action must identify one scenario/role binding, and malformed, missing-seed, duplicate, or ambiguous fixtures fail closed; fixture fields are never conflict-mutation slots. Do not declare fixtures for values the standard type derivation already supplies.
/Users/tiger/.codex/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/capabilities/actions-and-transactions.md:68:Before the single live Blueprint validation, trace every positive Handler branch from its input to every read and write. The published `handler.data_access` must include the complete locator chain, not only the final object: if a reward starts from a member and must find a card and then an account, publish the member/card/account reads or carry a truthful typed `card_id`/`account_id` input. For enum-driven branches such as membership, stored value, private training, refund, or transfer fees, require one positive scenario per branch and verify that the payload and capabilities can complete each branch.
